---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Drone LiDAR Surveys WA & Australia | DEMs, Contours, Point Clouds | Magtech Surveys"
  description="Drone LiDAR surveys for exploration logistics, earthworks, vegetation and terrain mapping across Australia. Ground-classified point clouds, bare-earth DEMs, DSMs and contours with CORS-controlled positioning."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">SERVICES / LIDAR</p>
      <span class="ramp-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h1>LiDAR surveys</h1>
      <p class="lede">Survey-grade terrain and canopy mapping, from single sites to multi-tenement programs.</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          LiDAR measures the ground directly, with enough pulses finding gaps in the canopy to
          map the surface beneath vegetation. That makes it the right tool where photogrammetry
          struggles: under canopy, over low-texture surfaces, and anywhere a true bare-earth
          terrain model matters. We fly it for exploration access and
          logistics planning, drill pad and earthworks design, drainage and hydrology, and
          vegetation structure mapping.
        </p>
        <p>
          Positioning is controlled by GNSS post-processing against CORS reference stations,
          giving reliable absolute accuracy even at remote sites with no established survey
          control. Point clouds are ground-classified and delivered with the derived products
          your engineers or geologists actually use.
        </p>
      </div>

      <table class="spec">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Typical accuracy</th><td>~5 cm absolute, 2&ndash;3 cm relative (surface and conditions dependent)</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Point density</th><td>Matched to purpose; we do not sell density beyond what improves accuracy</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Positioning</th><td>RTK with CORS post-processed control for remote sites</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Deliverables</th><td>Classified LAS/LAZ point cloud, bare-earth DEM, DSM, contours, hillshade. GeoTIFF and CAD-ready formats. GDA2020.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>LiDAR or photogrammetry?</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          They overlap, and we quote whichever suits the job rather than the one with the higher
          price. As a rule: vegetation, bare-earth terrain models or uniform surfaces like mown
          turf point to LiDAR. Visual records, orthomosaics and stockpile volumetrics on
          well-textured ground point to photogrammetry. If you are not sure, describe the end
          product you need and we will recommend the method, including telling you if the cheaper
          one is enough.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Cta />
</Base>
